Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Phase 4 checkpoint: keep the shipped seed baseline while
 the owner replaces it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Production-bootstrap edge case found while closing the Phase 4 checkpoint.

Before this change, zero QDN content rendered the full shipped seed bundle, but
the first published entity switched every kind to its QDN read result, so a kind
rendered only the entities discovery returned. The approved flow (§6.4) is that
the owner replaces the shipped content one entity at a time through the inline
editor, so after the first write every untouched shipped item — and with it the
only control that could ever publish that item — disappeared from the page.
Progressive editing could therefore not bootstrap the site at all.

The seed is now a per-entity, self-terminating baseline instead of a whole-kind
fallback (src/content/qdn-source.ts):

  - a shipped item is added only when discovery did not report its identifier at
    all, so a reported identifier (active, tombstoned, invalid or unreadable) is
    never replaced by its shipped default — "exists but failed to load" stays a
    reported failure, not a silent fallback, and a tombstone cannot resurrect;
  - a kind whose discovery failed or hit the page budget contributes no default,
    because a partial scan proves nothing about what exists (workspace guide
    qortal-architecture-and-data-integrity.md: "partial discovery MUST NOT grant
    authority");
  - the baseline ends by itself once every shipped identifier has been published
    or tombstoned; it is not a mode or a flag;
  - a new diagnostic reports how many shipped items still render this way.

Validated: tests/qdn-source.test.ts walks zero content -> first write -> reload ->
second write against the scripted node (tests/support/qdn.ts, the real bridge,
read and publish modules), proves untouched shipped items survive across both
reloads, proves a tombstoned shipped item is not resurrected, and proves the
baseline contributes nothing once every identifier is reported. Two of those
cases failed before this change. Full gate: tsc --noEmit, eslint ., prettier
--check . and 294 tests in 25 files pass; npm run build succeeds.

Not re-run: the Phase 4 owner-runtime run (Hub 3.0.3, staging
WEBSITE / Q-Website / default). This is a read-path merge rule only; the write,
owner-mode and inline-editing contracts and their runtime evidence are unchanged.

Executing agent: DeepSeek (Qortal platform implementation role)
